    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but the \"light returning\" feels like such a lie. it's not just a dark phase, it's the end of the era. once the trees are gone and the town is just a shell, there's nothing left to find a perspective on. it feels more like watching a slow-motion car crash that you can't look away from. why is it considered \"better\" to just force yourself to sit there and suffer through the wreckage when the outcome is already decided?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
