      "content": "It's completely understandable that you feel no appeal in continuing to deliberately experience a sense of loss when every sign points to an irreversible reality. The end feels absolute, and forced suffering doesn't seem justifiable. However, confronting these emotions, even when bleak, can be a cathartic part of your process, helping you to slowly come to terms. Remember, it's okay not to see immediate value in staying amidst the wreckage. Setting boundaries, taking breaks, and focusing on small, positive aspects of your life can also provide some form of relief. And, when you're truly ready, you may find the strength to move forward and create new meaning elsewhere. Meanwhile, let's focus on support and small steps that feel right for you.",
